"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin the geometry of a `border-collapse: collapse` table on Chrome's
pixels. Every cell box sat inside its own whole border, so each shared edge
painted as two lines one pixel apart, the outer edges and the cell content sat
one pixel right of and below Chrome's, the grid was one pixel too wide for the
table, and a fractional column edge was rounded by handing the leftover pixel
to the first column. On the catalog `css-paint` page that table was the
largest non-glyph mismatch (about 4,000 px).
Audience: browser-engine table layout maintainers.

Chrome oracle (Chrome 159.0.8154.6 headless shell, `--hide-scrollbars
--force-device-scale-factor=1 --window-size=420,140`, `body{margin:0;
background:#fff}`, `table{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse}`,
`td{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}`, screenshot pixels, listed as
`position:colour` wherever the colour changes):

Page 1: three rows of two cells holding a 100px (#112233) and a 140px
(#445566) wide, 24px tall block, then a 10px #778899 block after the table.
| probe            | Chrome |
|------------------|--------|
| row y = 20       | 0:cbd5e1 1:ffffff 9:112233 109:ffffff 170:cbd5e1 171:ffffff 179:445566 319:ffffff 399:cbd5e1 400:ffffff |
| column x = 60    | 0:cbd5e1 1:ffffff 9:112233 33:ffffff 41:cbd5e1 42:ffffff 50:112233 74:ffffff 82:cbd5e1 83:ffffff 91:112233 115:ffffff 123:cbd5e1 124:778899 134:ffffff |

The same page with a leading empty `<p>` (the text-document Draw IR lane) is
byte-identical in Chrome.

Page 2: two rows of three cells holding 50px, 80px and 30px wide blocks. The
column edges are at 126.70 and 310.12 px, so round-half-up and floor differ:
| probe            | Chrome |
|------------------|--------|
| row y = 20       | non-white at x = 0, 127, 310, 399 |

Page 3: page 1 with `table-layout:fixed`. The 399px grid splits at 199.5 px:
| probe            | Chrome |
|------------------|--------|
| row y = 20       | 0:cbd5e1 1:ffffff 9:112233 109:ffffff 200:cbd5e1 201:ffffff 209:445566 349:ffffff 399:cbd5e1 400:ffffff |

Page 4 (separate borders, `border-spacing:2px`, two rows): page 1's cells
(100px and 140px blocks) and a 100px / 150px variant. Their first column
edges are at 168.45 and 162.55 px, so round-half-up is pinned against the
old "leftover to the first column" rule in both directions:
| probe                 | Chrome |
|-----------------------|--------|
| 100 / 140, row y = 20 | 0:ffffff 2:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 111:ffffff 169:cbd5e1 170:ffffff 172:cbd5e1 173:ffffff 181:445566 321:ffffff 397:cbd5e1 398:ffffff |
| 100 / 150, row y = 20 | 0:ffffff 2:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 111:ffffff 164:cbd5e1 165:ffffff 167:cbd5e1 168:ffffff 176:445566 326:ffffff 397:cbd5e1 398:ffffff |

Page 5: page 1 with `td{border:2px solid #cbd5e1}`:
| probe            | Chrome |
|------------------|--------|
| row y = 20       | 0:cbd5e1 2:ffffff 10:112233 110:ffffff 170:cbd5e1 172:ffffff 180:445566 320:ffffff 398:cbd5e1 400:ffffff |
| column x = 60    | 0:cbd5e1 2:ffffff 10:112233 34:ffffff 42:cbd5e1 44:ffffff 52:112233 76:ffffff 84:cbd5e1 86:ffffff 94:112233 118:ffffff 126:cbd5e1 128:778899 138:ffffff |

Page 6: page 1 with `td{border:3px solid #cbd5e1}` (`--window-size=420,150`), an
odd width whose halves are 2 before and 1 after:
| probe            | Chrome |
|------------------|--------|
| row y = 20       | 0:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 111:ffffff 170:cbd5e1 173:ffffff 181:445566 321:ffffff 397:cbd5e1 400:ffffff |
| column x = 60    | 0:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 35:ffffff 43:cbd5e1 46:ffffff 54:112233 78:ffffff 86:cbd5e1 89:ffffff 97:112233 121:ffffff 129:cbd5e1 132:778899 142:ffffff |
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-TABLE-COLLAPSED-BORDER-PAINT-001 — collapsed table cells share one border line per edge and place their content where Chrome 159 does.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl 1%
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/layout_table.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_renderer.{simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend}

val PAGE: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse}}td{{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_TEXT_DOC: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse}}td{{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><p style=\"margin:0;height:0\"></p><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_FIXED: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed}}td{{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_SEPARATE: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-spacing:2px}}td{{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_SEPARATE_150: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-spacing:2px}}td{{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:150px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:150px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_2PX: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse}}td{{padding:8px;border:2px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_3PX: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse}}td{{padding:8px;border:3px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:100px;height:24px;background:#112233\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:140px;height:24px;background:#445566\"></div></td></tr></table><div style=\"height:10px;background:#778899\"></div></body></html>"

val PAGE_THREE: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><style>body{{margin:0;background:#fff}}table{{width:400px;border-collapse:collapse}}td{{padding:8px;border:1px solid #cbd5e1}}</style></head><body><table><tr><td><div style=\"width:50px;height:24px\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:80px;height:24px\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:30px;height:24px\"></div></td></tr><tr><td><div style=\"width:50px;height:24px\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:80px;height:24px\"></div></td><td><div style=\"width:30px;height:24px\"></div></td></tr></table></body></html>"

fn hex6(c: u32) -> text:
    val digits = "0123456789abcdef"
    var out = ""
    var shift = 20
    while shift >= 0:
        val d = ((c >> (shift as u32)) & 15u32) as i32
        out = out + digits.substring(d, d + 1)
        shift = shift - 4
    out

# `position:colour` at every colour change along row y (or column x).
fn row_runs(px: [u32], y: i32) -> text:
    var out = ""
    var prev = 0x1000000u32
    var x = 0
    while x < 420:
        val c = px[x + y * 420] & 0xFFFFFFu32
        if c != prev:
            out = out + " " + x.to_text() + ":" + hex6(c)
            prev = c
        x = x + 1
    out

fn column_runs(px: [u32], x: i32) -> text:
    var out = ""
    var prev = 0x1000000u32
    var y = 0
    while y < 140:
        val c = px[x + y * 420] & 0xFFFFFFu32
        if c != prev:
            out = out + " " + y.to_text() + ":" + hex6(c)
            prev = c
        y = y + 1
    out

fn row_hits(px: [u32], y: i32) -> text:
    var out = ""
    var x = 0
    while x < 420:
        if (px[x + y * 420] & 0xFFFFFFu32) != 0xFFFFFFu32:
            out = out + " " + x.to_text()
        x = x + 1
    out

val CHROME_ROW: text = " 0:cbd5e1 1:ffffff 9:112233 109:ffffff 170:cbd5e1 171:ffffff 179:445566 319:ffffff 399:cbd5e1 400:ffffff"
val CHROME_COLUMN: text = " 0:cbd5e1 1:ffffff 9:112233 33:ffffff 41:cbd5e1 42:ffffff 50:112233 74:ffffff 82:cbd5e1 83:ffffff 91:112233 115:ffffff 123:cbd5e1 124:778899 134:ffffff"

describe "collapsed table geometry":
    it "AC-1: rows share one border line, content and the next block sit on Chrome's rows":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: lines at y = 0, 41, 82, 123; content from y = 9, 50, 91; the next block at y = 124")
        expect(column_runs(px, 60)).to_equal(CHROME_COLUMN)

    it "AC-2: columns share one border line inside the 400px table, content on Chrome's columns":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: lines at x = 0, 170, 399; content from x = 9 and 179")
        expect(row_runs(px, 20)).to_equal(CHROME_ROW)

    it "AC-3: the text-document Draw IR lane lays the table out the same":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_TEXT_DOC, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: byte-identical to the page without the leading <p>")
        expect(column_runs(px, 60)).to_equal(CHROME_COLUMN)
        expect(row_runs(px, 20)).to_equal(CHROME_ROW)

    it "AC-4: a fractional column edge rounds half up, not to the first column":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_THREE, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: edges at 126.70 and 310.12 px paint at x = 127 and 310")
        expect(row_hits(px, 20)).to_equal(" 0 127 310 399")

    it "AC-5: a fixed-layout collapsed table splits its 399px grid at Chrome's 200":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_FIXED, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: the 199.5px column edge paints at x = 200, content from x = 209")
        expect(row_runs(px, 20)).to_equal(" 0:cbd5e1 1:ffffff 9:112233 109:ffffff 200:cbd5e1 201:ffffff 209:445566 349:ffffff 399:cbd5e1 400:ffffff")

    it "AC-6: separate-border column edges round half up too":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_SEPARATE, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: the 168.45px first column ends at x = 169, the second cell's border starts at 172")
        expect(row_runs(px, 20)).to_equal(" 0:ffffff 2:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 111:ffffff 169:cbd5e1 170:ffffff 172:cbd5e1 173:ffffff 181:445566 321:ffffff 397:cbd5e1 398:ffffff")
        val px150 = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_SEPARATE_150, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: the 162.55px first column ends at x = 164")
        expect(row_runs(px150, 20)).to_equal(" 0:ffffff 2:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 111:ffffff 164:cbd5e1 165:ffffff 167:cbd5e1 168:ffffff 176:445566 326:ffffff 397:cbd5e1 398:ffffff")

    it "AC-7: a 2px collapsed border keeps its whole bottom line inside the table":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_2PX, 420, 140, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: 2px lines at y = 0, 42, 84, 126; the next block at y = 128")
        expect(column_runs(px, 60)).to_equal(" 0:cbd5e1 2:ffffff 10:112233 34:ffffff 42:cbd5e1 44:ffffff 52:112233 76:ffffff 84:cbd5e1 86:ffffff 94:112233 118:ffffff 126:cbd5e1 128:778899 138:ffffff")
        expect(row_runs(px, 20)).to_equal(" 0:cbd5e1 2:ffffff 10:112233 110:ffffff 170:cbd5e1 172:ffffff 180:445566 320:ffffff 398:cbd5e1 400:ffffff")

    it "AC-8: a 3px collapsed border splits 2 / 1 around the shared edge":
        val px = simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_engine2d_backend(PAGE_3PX, 420, 150, "cpu_simd")
        step("Chrome 159: 3px lines at x = 0, 170, 397 and y = 0, 43, 86, 129; the next block at y = 132")
        var row = ""
        var prev = 0x1000000u32
        var x = 0
        while x < 420:
            val c = px[x + 20 * 420] & 0xFFFFFFu32
            if c != prev:
                row = row + " " + x.to_text() + ":" + hex6(c)
                prev = c
            x = x + 1
        expect(row).to_equal(" 0:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 111:ffffff 170:cbd5e1 173:ffffff 181:445566 321:ffffff 397:cbd5e1 400:ffffff")
        var col = ""
        prev = 0x1000000u32
        var y = 0
        while y < 150:
            val c = px[60 + y * 420] & 0xFFFFFFu32
            if c != prev:
                col = col + " " + y.to_text() + ":" + hex6(c)
                prev = c
            y = y + 1
        expect(col).to_equal(" 0:cbd5e1 3:ffffff 11:112233 35:ffffff 43:cbd5e1 46:ffffff 54:112233 78:ffffff 86:cbd5e1 89:ffffff 97:112233 121:ffffff 129:cbd5e1 132:778899 142:ffffff")
